dates, and \nreconciliation. Comfortable with production debugging, log analysis, and resolving live issues using Java, Spring Boot, \nand MySQL. \nEXPERIENCE \nNexabyte Innovations | Jr. Software Developer Noida · Jul 2025 – Present \n▸ Built PayIn and Payout platforms processing real-time UPI/IMPS/NEFT transactions using Java 17, Spring Boot, \nJPA, and MySQL. \n▸ Developed 15+ REST APIs for payment initiation, status tracking, and reconciliation — with proper request \nvalidation, structured error codes, and consistent response contracts. \n▸ Integrated third-party payment gateway APIs; handled webhook callbacks, managed timeout cases, and \nimplemented fallback logic for failed gateway responses. \n▸ Set up SLF4J/Logback logging to trace each transaction step (request received → DB update → gateway \nresponse), reducing mean time to diagnose production issues. \n▸ Resolved live production incidents (stuck transactions, duplicate callbacks, gateway mismatches) via log \ncorrelation; also optimised MySQL queries, reducing merchant dashboard load times. \n▸ Followed Agile practices: Maven builds, Git branching, sprint planning, standups, and peer code reviews. \nGlobwizards Technologies | Jr. Java Developer Remote · May 2024 – Jun 2025 \n▸ Built backend microservices for the John Deere Services Platform using Java and Spring Boot with clean REST API \ndesign. \n▸ Investigated production bugs via stack traces and log analysis; traced data-flow breakpoints and delivered fixes that \neliminated recurring failure patterns across service modules. \n▸ Validated 10+ APIs in Postman covering normal flows, edge cases, and error handling; collaborated with frontend \nteam to maintain stable API contracts. \nPerficient India | Intern – Consulting Bangalore · Jul 2023 – Sep 2023 \n▸ Built a login and role-based access control system using Spring Boot and Spring Security with JWT tokens and \nAPI-level authorisation. \n▸ Gained practical exposure to enterprise backend patterns: request handling, exception management, log reading, \nand database operations. \nPROJECTS \nPayIn Gateway & Payout Management Platform – Nexabyte Innovations 2025 \n▸ Designed and built end-to-end (frontend + backend): full payment flow from request intake → validation → gateway \ndispatch → callback → DB persistence → reconciliation. \n▸ Independently developed merchant authentication, request validation, transaction logging, and a real-time admin \ndashboard using JSP, Bootstrap, Spring Boot, and MySQL. \nCUPI – UPI-Based Payment App – Nexabyte Innovations 2026 \n▸ Sole developer (frontend + backend): built a UPI-style payment interface with payment initiation, transaction history, \nand status tracking using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Bootstrap, and Spring Boot. \nTECHNICAL SKILLS \n \nLanguages Java (8, 17), JavaScript, Python, HTML5, CSS3 \nBackend Spring Boot, Spring Security, JPA/Hibernate, REST APIs, Microservices \nDatabase MySQL, SQL query optimisation \nTools Maven, Git, Postman, JIRA, AWS (Certified Cloud Practitioner) \nPractices SLF4J/Logback logging, Production debugging, Payment lifecycle, Agile \nEDUCATION & CERTIFICATION \nB.Tech in Information Technology – KIET Group of Institutions, Delhi NCR 2024 \nAWS Certified Cloud Practitioner 2025 ','Srishti_Harit_Resume_2.pdf',312098,'2026-05-12 05:48:12.181000',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
